# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Mortgage Work — configuration (TEMPLATE)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. config.py reads `.env`; this
# template is the only one tracked in git. Never commit the real `.env`.
#
# Two blocks:
#
#   1. Runtime — non-secret, the only block a release build may ship (the
#      PyInstaller spec whitelists exactly these keys when bundling .env).
#   2. Dev-only — bare data stores and the debug viewers. Never packaged:
#      a release resolves its infrastructure credentials from the login
#      session instead (server/ delivers them, runtime_services.py reads).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Runtime (non-secret — safe to package)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Auth service — where this desktop app reaches email-code login. Local dev
# runs server/ on this box; a deployment points at the hosted instance.
AUTH_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9898

# Local agent service port (chat over WebSocket, spawned by app.py).
AGENT_PORT=8791

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Dev-only — data viewers + their data stores (never shipped)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This entire block is OPTIONAL: delete it and the app boots unchanged —
# app.py skips spawning the viewers, the Runtime panel greys their rows out.
# The whole stack is deployed on one host by rag-service/scripts/infra.sh and
# shares one password. Port split is counter-intuitive: FalkorDB owns 6379,
# plain Redis sits on 6380.

# falkordb viewer — graph store (Redis protocol + graph module)
FALKORDB_URI=falkordb://:<password>@<host>:6379
FALKORDB_VIEWER_PORT=8787

# rqlite viewer — basic auth, username fixed to "rag" by infra.sh
RQLITE_URI=http://rag:<password>@<host>:4001
RQLITE_VIEWER_PORT=9090

# qdrant viewer — REST API port; the OPENAI key powers its semantic search
QDRANT_URL=http://<host>:16333
QDRANT_API_KEY=<password>
QDRANT_VIEWER_PORT=8789
OPENAI_API_KEY=<openai-api-key>

# redis viewer — HOST/PORT/PASSWORD are assembled into a redis:// URL by config.py
REDIS_HOST=<host>
REDIS_PORT=6380
REDIS_PASSWORD=<password>
REDIS_VIEWER_PORT=8790

# Optional dev override: RAG/KG/web keys normally arrive with the login
# session (see the "Client service entitlement" section in server/.env.example).
# Set them here only when working against the stack without logging in
# (runtime_services.py falls back to these).
#RAG_SERVICE_URL=http://<host>:8000
#RAG_API_KEY=<rag-api-key>
#KG_SERVICE_URL=http://<host>:8001
#KG_API_KEY=<kg-api-key>
#FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=<firecrawl-api-key>
#JINA_API_KEY=<jina-api-key>
